  Result: The root cause of the KeyError issue in the gpt-engineer repository was found in the function `salvage_correct_hunks` in `gpt_engineer/core/default/steps.py`. The code assumed the presence of a previous filename key (`diff.filename_pre`) in the current files dictionary, which caused the crash when this key did not exist. I fixed this by adding a presence check before accessing the dictionary to prevent the KeyError and handle missing keys gracefully.

